{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Also My hand.</b> The left, by way of simile." "And He mentioned the right hand together with the heavens because they are more honored than the earth." "Now the sense of \"also\" in \"for I am the first and I am the last\" is that I created everything." "And the sense of <b>spanned.</b> [Like] which I spanned and made grow (Lamentations 2:22). And some say He measured the heavens with a span, and from this verse the commentators learned that the heavens and the earth were created together, neither preceding the other. According to the plain sense: I made them, and at the time I call them to fulfill My will, they both stand before Me as servants; like it: \"for Your judgments stood today\" (Psalms 119:91), for how can one call to that which is not? [i.e., how can HaShem call to that which is not?]"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:37.452572800Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}